    "status": "present",
    "value": "A city map is a grid of strings. 'S' is the start, 'D' the destination, 'X' a blocked cell, and a digit d marks a cell served by transport mode modes[d-1]. You may move up, down, left or right. Using exactly one mode for the whole trip, you may only step on cells of that mode's digit (plus D at the end). Each step that leaves a cell of the mode costs that mode's time and cost; leaving S is free. Among the modes that can reach D, choose the one with the smallest total time, then the smallest total cost, then the lowest index, and return its name. Return an empty string if no single mode reaches D."
  },
